Clicking the title bar on Windows doesn't freeze animations.

A caption press the app lets through goes to DefWindowProc, and Windows'
move loop waits for the pointer to move before it pumps any messages:
about half a second for a click that never moves, the whole hold for a
press held still. No WM_PAINT, timer or posted task reaches gpui in that
time, so everything animated stops. The drag grips stall the same way,
since start_window_move sends its press through the same handler.

Posting a WM_MOUSEMOVE with an lparam of 0 before handing the press over
wakes the loop at once, the workaround winit has carried since its #839.
A double click toggles maximize without a move loop, so it's split off and
never gets the nudge, and a nudge still queued after a refused move is
dropped before gpui reads it as a pointer jump to the corner.

zed main still hands the press straight to DefWindowProc (checked October
2026), so this stays through the next bump unless that changes.

Diffed against the tree with every earlier patch applied.

--- a/src/platform/windows/events.rs
+++ b/src/platform/windows/events.rs
@@ -64,9 +64,15 @@
             // Treat double click as a second single click, since we track the double clicks ourselves.
             // If you don't interact with any elements, this will fall through to the windows default
             // behavior of toggling whether the window is maximized.
-            WM_NCLBUTTONDBLCLK | WM_NCLBUTTONDOWN => {
+            WM_NCLBUTTONDBLCLK => {
                 self.handle_nc_mouse_down_msg(handle, MouseButton::Left, wparam, lparam)
             }
+            // rox patch: split from the double click, which never starts a move
+            // loop, so only a press that does gets the nudge. See
+            // handle_caption_press.
+            WM_NCLBUTTONDOWN => self
+                .handle_nc_mouse_down_msg(handle, MouseButton::Left, wparam, lparam)
+                .or_else(|| self.handle_caption_press(handle, wparam, lparam)),
             WM_NCRBUTTONDOWN => {
                 self.handle_nc_mouse_down_msg(handle, MouseButton::Right, wparam, lparam)
             }
@@ -1094,6 +1100,39 @@
